1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,365
Time for K-Culture. And I'm told
someone here is very excited.

2
00:00:05,365 --> 00:00:08,660
Offbeat, our K-pop and entertainment desk.

3
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:14,850
I'm not excited. I'm calm.
I'm so calm. FIN.K.L IS BACK!

4
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,160
There it is.

5
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:19,630
Offbeat, you've been
vibrating since this morning.

6
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:23,580
That's not vibrating. That's
my heart doing choreography.

7
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:28,170
Medically speaking, he's fine.
Emotionally, he's a disaster.

8
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:33,320
I made a vision board. It's just
the word "FIN.K.L" in twelve fonts.

9
00:00:33,670 --> 00:00:34,950
Is that a vision?

10
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:36,580
It's a lifestyle.

11
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:40,690
For viewers who didn't grow up
in the nineties: who is Fin.K.L?

12
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,476
First-generation K-pop royalty.

13
00:00:43,476 --> 00:00:47,091
A four-member girl group
that debuted in 1998.

14
00:00:47,091 --> 00:00:49,920
Their big rival back then was S.E.S.

15
00:00:50,270 --> 00:00:53,550
Nineteen ninety-eight. So,
K-pop before it went global?

16
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:57,420
Back when "going viral" meant
staying home with a cold.

17
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:00,170
And "streaming" meant a leaky pipe.

18
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,524
Back when your phone flipped open,

19
00:01:02,524 --> 00:01:06,120
and your whole personality lived
on a website called Cyworld.

20
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:09,350
I had a MySpace page.
It was a crime scene.

21
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:13,140
Let's meet them. Starting with Lee Hyori.

22
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:17,560
Lee Hyori went solo and became
one of Korea's biggest stars,

23
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,730
and a variety-show favorite too.

24
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,080
Next, Ock Joo-hyun.

25
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:25,870
She became one of Korea's
top musical theater stars.

26
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:31,260
Singing and acting live, every
night. I can barely finish one shift.

27
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:32,730
Lee Jin?

28
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:35,240
Lee Jin moved into acting.

29
00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:36,790
And Sung Yuri.

30
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,072
Sung Yuri became a drama lead,

31
00:01:39,072 --> 00:01:42,420
in hits like "Romance Town"
and "Feast of the Gods."

32
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:48,210
One pop queen, one stage star, two
actresses. Four careers, one group chat.

33
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:52,640
Skills: singing, acting, dancing,
and surviving a camper van.

34
00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:58,590
Weakness: none. Hobbies:
none. Fear: Wi-Fi.

35
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:01,607
Now the news. On September twenty-first,

36
00:02:01,607 --> 00:02:06,140
their agency announced that all
four members will return as a group.

37
00:02:06,490 --> 00:02:10,330
Four members. One agency. Zero spoilers.

38
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:14,360
Wait. When was the last time
all four did something together?

39
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:18,825
The last full-group release
was a digital single in 2005.

40
00:02:18,825 --> 00:02:23,590
It was called "Forever Fin.K.L."
After that, the group went quiet.

41
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:29,060
Forever lasted twenty-one years.
That's one damn long intermission.

42
00:02:29,410 --> 00:02:32,930
Somebody born in 2005 is now twenty-one.

43
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:37,040
Old enough to vote, drink, and be
disappointed by group projects.

44
00:02:37,390 --> 00:02:43,054
And a fan who was fourteen in 2005
is thirty-five now. They have jobs.

45
00:02:43,054 --> 00:02:44,430
And credit cards.

46
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:46,940
Oh no. That's the real news.

47
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:50,330
They did get together in 2019, right?

48
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:54,136
A TV show called "Camping
Club." They made music for it.

49
00:02:54,136 --> 00:02:57,160
But that was a one-off,
built around a broadcast.

50
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:58,870
What was the show about?

51
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:02,919
Four old friends, one camper
van, a road trip around Korea.

52
00:03:02,919 --> 00:03:05,364
They talked about life after the group,

53
00:03:05,364 --> 00:03:09,940
and whether to perform together again
for their twenty-first anniversary.

54
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:13,970
A road trip with a very big
question in the glove box.

55
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:18,560
It premiered in July 2019 to
strong ratings. People loved it.

56
00:03:18,910 --> 00:03:23,070
So, a high school reunion.
With cameras. And tents.

57
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:27,134
This time is different.
Their agency says no one-off.

58
00:03:27,134 --> 00:03:31,900
About two years of meeting fans,
with music, performances, and more.

59
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:33,450
More, meaning what?

60
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:38,768
Documentaries, variety shows,
exhibitions, official merchandise,

61
00:03:38,768 --> 00:03:41,640
brand collabs, ads, and fan projects.

62
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:46,710
Translation: there will be a mug.
And damn right I'm buying the mug.

63
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,140
Nobody's buying just one mug.

64
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:52,850
They'll buy the mug, a second
mug, and the mug's cousin.

65
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,040
The mug has a cousin?

66
00:03:55,390 --> 00:03:59,310
Everything has a cousin. It's
called a limited edition.

67
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:01,900
Let's pitch some documentary titles.

68
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:03,930
"Fin.K.L: The Sequel."

69
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,720
"Fast and Fin.K.L."

70
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:08,310
"Fin.K.L and the Temple of Doom."

71
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:11,140
"Fin.K.L Two: Electric Boogaloo."

72
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:14,450
Please stop. That is not
how any of this works.

73
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,400
I wrote a fanfic about it!

74
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:17,870
...Of course you did.

75
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:22,940
It's four hundred pages. It
has a prologue. And a map.

76
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:24,650
A map?!

77
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,480
Fandom lore needs geography, Doctor.

78
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:30,710
Offbeat, you used to train
to be an idol, right?

79
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:33,460
I was this close to debuting.

80
00:04:33,810 --> 00:04:34,450
How close?

81
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:38,880
Close enough to know a practice
room smells like sweat and ambition.

82
00:04:39,230 --> 00:04:41,470
And you were half a beat late.

83
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,980
Half a beat. Every time.

84
00:04:44,330 --> 00:04:47,210
Okay. Let's play Reunion Bingo.

85
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:50,920
Free space: somebody
cries. Everybody cries.

86
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:54,790
Square two: somebody says,
"We never really left."

87
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:58,660
Square three: a brand announces
a collab within the hour.

88
00:04:59,010 --> 00:05:03,090
Square four: a coworker
says, "My mom loves them."

89
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:06,960
Bingo. I won a game I
didn't know I was playing.

90
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:09,630
Why does this matter outside Korea?

91
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:12,942
Because it shows how Korean fandom works.

92
00:05:12,942 --> 00:05:17,637
Fans don't just grow up with a
group. They grow old with a group.

93
00:05:17,637 --> 00:05:19,660
In a very loud, glowing way.

94
00:05:20,010 --> 00:05:20,970
Glowing?

95
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:24,121
Light sticks. Every group
has an official one.

96
00:05:24,121 --> 00:05:28,200
Thousands of them in the dark look
like a galaxy that bought merch.

97
00:05:28,550 --> 00:05:30,877
In America, we get nostalgia tours.

98
00:05:30,877 --> 00:05:33,670
A guy in a leather jacket, a lot of knees.

99
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:35,060
Knees?

100
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:39,250
Doctor's observation. Reunion
tours are mostly knees.

101
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:42,880
Not these knees. These
knees have a choreographer.

102
00:05:43,230 --> 00:05:47,310
Anyway. The comeback is
real. I'm calm. I'm calm!

103
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:49,020
He is not calm.

104
00:05:49,370 --> 00:05:52,170
Which group would you bring
back? Tell us in the comments.

105
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:58,180
Next, the K-pop calendar.
Because in October, it's a lot.

106
00:05:58,530 --> 00:06:04,050
I made a spreadsheet. It has colors.
It has tabs. It has a tab for the tabs.

107
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:08,320
Doctor's note: very healthy
hobby. I'm proud of the tabs.

108
00:06:08,670 --> 00:06:13,230
Quick vocabulary check. In
K-pop, what does "comeback" mean?

109
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:17,900
A new release. New music,
new concept, new promotions.

110
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:20,250
So you can come back without ever leaving?

111
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:24,520
That's the best part. You can come
back on Monday, and again in March.

112
00:06:24,870 --> 00:06:25,507
In America,

113
00:06:25,507 --> 00:06:29,910
a comeback means you disappeared for
ten years and a reality show saved you.

114
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:32,340
So how many new releases this month?

115
00:06:32,690 --> 00:06:36,880
One tracker lists fifty-two
scheduled for October.

116
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:41,490
Albums, mini albums, EPs,
from groups and solo artists.

117
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:44,960
Fifty-two? October has thirty-one days.

118
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:48,670
So that's more than one new
release every single day.

119
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:52,620
I have fewer appointments
than that. And I'm a doctor.

120
00:06:52,970 --> 00:06:56,764
Okay, let's go. This week,
according to that tracker.

121
00:06:56,764 --> 00:06:59,770
October sixth: KickFlip, X:IN, and Yesung.

122
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:03,400
X:IN. Is that a band or a Wi-Fi password?

123
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:09,590
October seventh: ONEW and ZICO team
up. The song is called "Tic Tac Toe."

124
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:12,980
Finally, a K-pop song
I can play on a napkin.

125
00:07:13,330 --> 00:07:17,404
ONEW is from SHINee, one of
K-pop's veteran boy groups.

126
00:07:17,404 --> 00:07:21,330
ZICO is a rapper and producer
who started in Block B.

127
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:25,440
A singer and a rapper. Is
this a duet or a negotiation?

128
00:07:25,790 --> 00:07:29,966
Two seasoned pros. I trained
for years in a practice room.

129
00:07:29,966 --> 00:07:31,550
They actually debuted.

130
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:39,180
October eighth: N.Flying, plus YUQI of
i-dle with a mini album called "27."

131
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:42,810
Just "27"? The whole title is a number?

132
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,920
That's it. Minimalism.

133
00:07:45,270 --> 00:07:48,790
I respect a short title. Like
my patients' attention span.

134
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:51,813
Quick K-pop culture question.

135
00:07:51,813 --> 00:07:57,620
Why do idols get photographed
just for walking into an airport?

136
00:07:57,970 --> 00:08:00,432
Because airport fashion is a thing.

137
00:08:00,432 --> 00:08:04,370
Photographers wait there, and
the walk becomes a runway.

138
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:08,160
I walk through airports all the
time. Nobody photographs me.

139
00:08:08,510 --> 00:08:09,470
Give it time.

140
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:12,525
Next week. October twelfth:

141
00:08:12,525 --> 00:08:20,540
Sung Han-bin of ZEROBASEONE makes his
solo debut with an EP called "DEAD:ALIVE."

142
00:08:20,890 --> 00:08:25,130
Dead or alive? That's not a
title. That's a triage question.

143
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:32,680
K-pop idols also learn heart signs.
Finger heart, arm heart, big heart.

144
00:08:33,030 --> 00:08:35,830
I know one heart. The anatomical one.

145
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:40,020
Also on the twelfth: Xdinary
Heroes with "IMPULSE."

146
00:08:40,370 --> 00:08:44,152
And near the end of the
month, October twenty-third:

147
00:08:44,152 --> 00:08:46,770
LISA of BLACKPINK with "PRESS PLAY."

148
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:50,000
Finally, a title that's
also an instruction.

149
00:08:50,350 --> 00:08:52,052
October twenty-sixth:

150
00:08:52,052 --> 00:08:56,510
ILLIT with "BREAK EVEN," and
IVE with "Looks Can Kill."

151
00:08:56,860 --> 00:09:01,020
"Break Even." The only financial
goal my clinic has ever hit.

152
00:09:01,370 --> 00:09:05,930
ILLIT is one of K-pop's newer
groups. They debuted in 2024.

153
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:11,400
And "Looks Can Kill" is basically a
warning label. I'll sign the waiver.

154
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:15,389
And IVE is going full superhero movie.

155
00:09:15,389 --> 00:09:22,189
Six members, six hero names: Captain
Purple, Wonder Green, Jean Yellow,

156
00:09:22,189 --> 00:09:25,350
Bat Pink, Super Blue, Spider Red.

157
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:27,940
Bat Pink. I'd read that comic.

158
00:09:28,290 --> 00:09:33,090
Pre-release is October nineteenth. The
album comes out October twenty-sixth.

159
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:34,922
And it's a close race!

160
00:09:34,922 --> 00:09:38,560
IVE on the inside, LISA
coming up fast on the outside!

161
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:40,670
Please stop commentating.

162
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:42,620
I can't. It's live.

163
00:09:42,970 --> 00:09:46,570
Offbeat, how do fans
survive fifty-two releases?

164
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:50,217
Simple. You stream. You
vote. You buy the album.

165
00:09:50,217 --> 00:09:53,240
Then you buy the other
version of the album.

166
00:09:53,590 --> 00:09:55,670
The same album? Again?

167
00:09:56,020 --> 00:09:59,780
Different cover. Different
photocard. It's called collecting.

168
00:10:00,130 --> 00:10:02,690
So that's where the
mug's cousin comes from.

169
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:05,360
The mug's cousin has a photocard.

170
00:10:05,710 --> 00:10:07,470
Damn. I knew it.

171
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:10,811
Fun fact: if you listened
to one release a day,

172
00:10:10,811 --> 00:10:13,420
October would take you nearly two months.

173
00:10:13,770 --> 00:10:16,650
That's without sleeping. Or repeats.

174
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,880
Repeats are mandatory.
That's the whole point.

175
00:10:20,230 --> 00:10:21,830
Who's your pick of the month?

176
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:27,140
I can't choose. I love them all equally.
Ask me again after I've heard them.

177
00:10:27,490 --> 00:10:31,250
Tell us your pick in the comments. And
please tell Offbeat to drink water.

178
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:34,560
I'm calm. I'm hydrated. I'm calm!

179
00:10:34,910 --> 00:10:37,710
That was K-Culture. Thanks for watching.

180
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:39,100
I'm calm.

181
00:10:39,450 --> 00:10:41,770
He is holding a light stick in each hand.

182
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:45,000
That's the show. Subscribe,
and we'll see you next week.

183
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:48,310
Bye! Drink water! I'm calm!

184
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:51,460
Stay curious. Keep your lenses clean.
